WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.775
The paper's central contribution is a simple,

00:00:02.855 --> 00:00:07.978
drop-in two-sample test for networks that swaps
graph moments for graph cumulants.

00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:12.166
Using theory, controlled simulation, and real
biological networks,

00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:19.019
the authors show this swap consistently increases
statistical power without changing the computational cost.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:25.808
They further show that the cumulant test statistic
tracks a known chi-squared distribution remarkably well,

00:00:25.888 --> 00:00:28.029
even with only a handful of graphs,

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:31.518
so false-positive rates can be controlled analytically.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:36.848
Strikingly, the cumulant test even works when just
one graph is observed per sample,

00:00:36.928 --> 00:00:39.640
a regime where the moment test is undefined.
